## Claim
Text: "US President Trump instructed his administration to halt funding of the World Health Organization while a review was conducted to assess the World Health Organization’s role regarding the spread of coronavirus."
Claim date: September 01, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### Did Donald Trump, while serving as President of the United States, formally direct the US government to suspend funding to the World Health Organization in 2020?
Answer: Yes, Donald Trump formally directed the US government to suspend funding to the World Health Organization in 2020. As reported by the BMJ, he stated during a press conference on April 14, 2020: "Today I’m instructing my administration to halt funding to the WHO while a review is conducted to assess its role in severely mismanaging and covering up the spread of the coronavirus."

Source URL: https://www.bmj.com/content/369/bmj.m1502

### Was the suspension of US funding to the World Health Organization officially linked by the Trump administration to an assessment of the WHO's role in the COVID-19 pandemic response?
Answer: Yes, the suspension of US funding to the WHO was explicitly and officially linked by the Trump administration to an assessment of the WHO's role in the COVID-19 pandemic response. As President Trump stated at a White House news conference: "I am directing my administration to halt funding while a review is conducted to assess the World Health Organization's role in severely mismanaging and covering up the spread of the coronavirus." He further specified that a decision on resuming funding would be made after the review, which he said would last 60 to 90 days, making the connection between the funding halt and the pandemic-related assessment direct and official.

Source URL: https://www.bbc.com/news/world-us-canada-52289056

### On what specific date in 2020 did President Trump announce or instruct the halt of US funding to the World Health Organization?
Answer: President Trump announced the halt of US funding to the World Health Organization on **April 14, 2020**. As reported, "Speaking at a press conference on 14 April, Trump said, 'Today I’m instructing my administration to halt funding to the WHO...'"

Source URL: https://www.bmj.com/content/369/bmj.m1502

