## Final Judgement
Based on the recorded evidence, the key finding is that President Donald Trump publicly and explicitly announced on April 14, 2020, that he was instructing his administration to halt funding to the World Health Organization (WHO). He directly and officially stated this was to be done "while a review was conducted" to assess the WHO's role in "severely mismanaging and covering up the spread of the coronavirus." The announcement is well-documented across multiple reliable news sources.

The evidence clearly establishes that the claim's core elements—1) the instruction to halt funding, 2) its linkage to a review, and 3) the stated purpose of that review—are factual and supported. There is no contradictory information in the record that disputes these points. The claim's wording closely mirrors President Trump's own statements as reported.

